appropriating money for the Reed Avenue

00:09:45.519 --> 00:09:49.279 align:start position:19%
corridor project.
&gt;&gt; All right. All right. Is there anybody

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:53.760 align:start position:19%
in the audience would like to speak
about the city council's intention to

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:59.560 align:start position:19%
appropriate $5 million for the Reed
Avenue corridor project if and when the

00:09:55.839 --> 00:09:59.560 align:start position:19%
railroad gives us permission.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:09.040 align:start position:19%
Jim, welcome. Mr. Mayor, thank you. Good
evening, Mr. Mayor, council members. For

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:13.120 align:start position:19%
the record, my name is Jim Walter. I
serve as the president and CEO of Visit

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:15.920 align:start position:19%
Cheyenne, our community's destination
marketing organization. and I also

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:20.560 align:start position:19%
currently chair the greenway advisory
committee and I'm a W three resident.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:24.720 align:start position:19%
I'm here tonight in support of moving
the Reed Avenue corridor project

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:28.720 align:start position:19%
forward. From my perspective, there's
three reasons to consider a yes vote.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:32.880 align:start position:19%
First, this is the kind of project we
should find a way to fund. It's

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:35.680 align:start position:19%
destination defining. I commend council
for finding a path forward without

00:10:34.399 --> 00:10:39.279 align:start position:19%
placing an additional burden on
taxpayers. If there's a path to an

00:10:37.839 --> 00:10:43.360 align:start position:19%
advanced and important piece of city
infrastructure forward without going

00:10:41.279 --> 00:10:47.760 align:start position:19%
back to residents for more, that's worth
serious consideration.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:52.079 align:start position:19%
Secondly, this project aligns with the
Cheyenne tourism master plan. On page

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:55.760 align:start position:19%
12, the plan specifically calls out the
Reed Avenue corridor as part of

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:58.959 align:start position:19%
developing the west edge of downtown.
That same section also highlights

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:03.040 align:start position:19%
improving downtown infrastructure and
appearance as a priority because those

00:11:01.279 --> 00:11:07.760 align:start position:19%
investments shape how residents and
visitors experience Cheyenne.

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:11.360 align:start position:19%
Third, a stronger and more vibrant
downtown attracts continued private

00:11:09.519 --> 00:11:15.120 align:start position:19%
investment. We've seen a lot of private
investment on the West Edge already.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:18.800 align:start position:19%
Public infrastructure is often what
gives the private sector the confidence

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:22.800 align:start position:19%
to move forward. When we improve access,
appearance, and connectivity, we create

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:27.440 align:start position:19%
conditions for more retail, lodging,
dining, housing, and other business

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:31.040 align:start position:19%
development. Here at Visit Cheyenne, we
believe downtown matters because it's

00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:34.959 align:start position:19%
one of the clearest expressions of our
community to visitors and residents

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:38.560 align:start position:19%
alike. Reed Avenue is not just a
corridor project. It's a signal about

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:44.760 align:start position:19%
where Cheyenne is heading. Thank you for
your consideration.

00:11:39.839 --> 00:11:44.760 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Well said, Jim. Thank you. Anybody else?

00:11:47.279 --> 00:11:53.040 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Mr. Escoel,
&gt;&gt; Mr. Mayor, the recommendation of the

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:56.000 align:start position:19%
finance committee is to approve on third
and final reading and I so move.

