&gt;&gt; Mr. Mayor, I think that uh what uh the
visit Cheyenne just said pretty much

00:12:09.519 --> 00:12:18.639 align:start position:19%
covered it, but I want to emphasize this
is following through on a long planned

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:23.839 align:start position:19%
and a project that was on the ballot
some years ago. We're now going to fund

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:28.079 align:start position:19%
it. And I think that's very important
and hopefully it'll be part of the

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:37.440 align:start position:19%
discussion of the sixth penny because
this is uh the followup to that project.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:44.079 align:start position:19%
So um I think we're ready to uh move on
it and I expect the railroad to finally

00:12:40.959 --> 00:12:49.120 align:start position:19%
approve and we can actually support the
businesses that have invested. Thank

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:52.800 align:start position:19%
you.
&gt;&gt; Dr. Aldridge. Mayor Collins through you.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:57.279 align:start position:19%
I know there's been a lot of
conversation about whether we should

00:12:54.800 --> 00:13:01.920 align:start position:19%
take $5 million from our general reserve
to fund this uh Reed Avenue corridor

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:05.519 align:start position:19%
project. I'm going to be a yes vote
tonight. And the reason for that is

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:13.360 align:start position:19%
because this is a a project that was
started um prior to my term on uh

00:13:09.279 --> 00:13:17.120 align:start position:19%
council um five years ago. And there was
a commitment, I believe, that the voters

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:21.920 align:start position:19%
of Cheyenne voted to support this
project on that six penny ballot. and

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:25.920 align:start position:19%
the money I think just didn't go far
enough quite honestly. Um there were

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:30.639 align:start position:19%
some missteps, definitely some things
that we could have done better probably

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:36.560 align:start position:19%
as a city government. Um but I think
that over time the expense has also

00:13:33.279 --> 00:13:40.880 align:start position:19%
increased dramatically um with increased
pricing and um materials and things. I

00:13:39.519 --> 00:13:44.160 align:start position:19%
think that there's also been a lot of
footwork that's been done and a lot of

00:13:42.639 --> 00:13:50.639 align:start position:19%
foundational work that's been laid with
the um BNSF railroad um in order to get

00:13:48.399 --> 00:13:55.440 align:start position:19%
this far. And the reason I'll be voting
to support this tonight is because this

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:59.920 align:start position:19%
is contingent upon an an approved plan
by the BNSF railroad. If they don't

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:03.199 align:start position:19%
approve the plan and give the final
okay, this money will not be spent from

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:06.079 align:start position:19%
the general reserves. So, for that
reason, I will be a yes vote tonight.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:10.639 align:start position:19%
But I wanted to make sure that people
understood that this is a project that

00:14:08.079 --> 00:14:15.199 align:start position:19%
was started early on and that we have a
commitment I believe to finish a project

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:21.120 align:start position:19%
that voters voted on and expected us to
continue uh through completion.

