00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:19.680 align:start position:19%
&gt;&gt; Good evening and welcome.
&gt;&gt; Good evening. Thanks for having me,

00:40:17.280 --> 00:40:23.599 align:start position:19%
Jordan community member. I'm here to
speak in opposition to the proposed

00:40:21.599 --> 00:40:27.599 align:start position:19%
annex. We keep hearing that this will
benefit the neighbors and the broader

00:40:25.520 --> 00:40:32.000 align:start position:19%
community. But the biggest issue many
residents have tonight isn't just the

00:40:29.359 --> 00:40:36.560 align:start position:19%
project itself. It's trust. A lot of
residents no longer believe their input

00:40:34.079 --> 00:40:40.320 align:start position:19%
actually changes anything. People show
up, they send emails, they speak during

00:40:38.480 --> 00:40:43.839 align:start position:19%
public comment,
and then decisions move forward exactly

00:40:42.160 --> 00:40:47.520 align:start position:19%
the way they seem to be planned from the
beginning. Now comments on social media

00:40:45.599 --> 00:40:51.200 align:start position:19%
have even been disabled. When that
happens over and over again, public

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:55.520 align:start position:19%
participation starts to feel less like
it matters and more like a box that just

00:40:53.440 --> 00:40:58.720 align:start position:19%
needs to be checked. Now, we're told
that the annexation will help the area

00:40:57.040 --> 00:41:03.520 align:start position:19%
by bringing city fire and police
services. But that claim raises another

00:41:01.040 --> 00:41:06.800 align:start position:19%
question about capacity. The city has
struggled even to address issues like

00:41:05.280 --> 00:41:10.400 align:start position:19%
compensation for the firefighters who
already serve this community. If

00:41:08.480 --> 00:41:14.079 align:start position:19%
supporting the people who are currently
protecting this city has been difficult,

00:41:12.480 --> 00:41:18.000 align:start position:19%
it's reasonable for the residents to
question how expanding the city's

00:41:15.599 --> 00:41:22.000 align:start position:19%
responsibilities will work in practice.
At the same time, we've seen the county

00:41:20.240 --> 00:41:25.680 align:start position:19%
sheriff's office picking up more of the
workload created by the recent

00:41:23.440 --> 00:41:29.520 align:start position:19%
annexations. They've stepped in to help
cover the gaps, and they're doing that

00:41:27.680 --> 00:41:33.359 align:start position:19%
without receiving additional benefits or
resources from the city for that effort.

00:41:31.440 --> 00:41:37.440 align:start position:19%
So when the city says annexation will
improve services, many residents

00:41:35.440 --> 00:41:42.000 align:start position:19%
understandably want to know how. That
promise will be fulfilled when the

00:41:39.200 --> 00:41:46.319 align:start position:19%
existing system is already under strain.
Leadership requires more than announcing

00:41:44.640 --> 00:41:51.359 align:start position:19%
projects and asking the public to trust
the outcome. It requires transparency,

00:41:48.960 --> 00:41:55.359 align:start position:19%
honesty about impacts, and willingness
to listen when the community raises

00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:58.319 align:start position:19%
legitimate concerns. Tonight, you have
the opportunity to show the residents

00:41:56.880 --> 00:42:03.640 align:start position:19%
that their voices matter before
decisions are finalized, not after.

00:42:00.400 --> 00:42:03.640 align:start position:19%
Thank you.

